&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:13.0pt;mso-bidi-font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:&amp;quot;Arial&amp;quot;,sans-serif;mso-fareast-font-family:&amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;;
mso-ansi-language:EN-GB;mso-fareast-language:EN-US;mso-bidi-language:AR-SA&quot;&gt;The
retention of the link between the main dwelling and the outbuilding, by reason
of its height, massing and continuous length across the rear garden, results in
an overly dominant and visually intrusive form of development. It erodes the
openness of the garden and fails to respect the character, scale and pattern of
development of the host property and surrounding area. The proposal is
therefore contrary to the National Planning Policy Framework (2024), London
Plan Policies D3 and D4, and Merton Local Plan Policies D12.1, D12.3 and D12.4.&lt;br&gt;
&lt;!--[if !supportLineBreakNewLine]--&gt;&lt;br&gt;
&lt;!--[endif]--&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
